      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{3x+5}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let $u=3x+5.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u,$ solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{3x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =1\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+5|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
